st rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Laurel Lee (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Florida's 15th District leans Republican by about nine points, and incumbent Laurel Lee enters the general election having been renominated after a primary challenge from Steve Champion. She has raised roughly $2.3 million and holds about $2 million on hand, while Democratic nominee Robert People has raised about $40,000 and reports only a few thousand dollars in the bank. National House Democrats removed the district from their target list over the summer.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals and expert judgment. Eight of ten ratings outlets call the race Safe or Solid Republican, with two rating it Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Lee roughly a 93 percent chance. Redistricting made the seat more Republican, and the broader environment this year favors the party. The race appears out of reach for Democrats absent a major unforeseen shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -10.97}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0254, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0409, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0544, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0182, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0196, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0404, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0628, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0307, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.018, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0317,